@startuml
!include https://static.visual-paradigm.com/web/resources/plantuml-stdlib/themes/vp.puml

title Auth - Reset Password

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam activityFontName Arial
skinparam activityFontSize 14
skinparam activityBorderThickness 1.5
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam ArrowColor #222222
skinparam SwimlaneBorderColor #222222
skinparam SwimlaneBorderThickness 2
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #7DD3FC
  BorderColor #2563EB
  DiamondBackgroundColor #7DD3FC
  DiamondBorderColor #2563EB
  StartColor #111827
  EndColor #FFFFFF
}

|Guest|
start
note right
Precondition:
The user is not signed in.

Postcondition:
The password is replaced, the code is used up and all
refresh tokens are revoked. The user signs in again.
end note
:Choose forgot password and enter the email;
:Request the reset code;
|System|
:If the email belongs to an enabled account within the limits (60 s apart, 5 codes per hour), create a 6-digit code valid for 15 minutes and email it;
:Always return the same success response, even for an unknown email;
|Guest|
repeat
:Enter the email, the code and the new password;
:Submit the password reset;
|System|
if (The system fails while processing the request?) then (Yes)
  :Return the system error;
  |Guest|
  :View the system error;
  stop
else (No)
endif
|System|
:Check the latest code is unexpired, unused, under 5 wrong attempts and correct;
backward :Return the same invalid-code error and count the wrong attempt;
repeat while (The code is wrong, expired,\nused or out of attempts?) is (Yes) not (No)
:Change the password, invalidate the codes and revoke all refresh tokens;
|Guest|
:View the result and sign in again;
stop

@enduml
